{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-quantum-gauge-group","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Definition","doco:Section"],"label":"def:quantum-gauge-group","kind":"definition","title":"Quantum Gauge Group","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-substrate-parameter"],"tags":["gauge-group","quantum-group"],"leanRef":"qou:QOU.QuantumGaugeGroup","text":"quantum-gauge-group.md","leanSource":"quantum-gauge-group.lean","provenance":"authored","html":"<p><a id=\"def:quantum-gauge-group\"></a>\n<strong>Definition.</strong> <em>Quantum Gauge Group</em></p>\n<p>The reconstructed Hopf algebra <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">H = \\mathrm{End}^{\\otimes}(\\tau)</code> gives the <strong>quantum gauge group</strong> <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">G_q = \\mathrm{SU}_q(2)</code>, with <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">q</code> categorically fixed by the symmetric braiding eigenvalue. Over a spacetime <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">M</code>, this defines a local field of quantum groups <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\{G_{q(p)}\\}</code>.</p>\n"}
